# Adapted coordinates for the native 120-dimensional M₁₂ tensor model

The native point order is 0,...,11; the heart basis consists of e_i + e_11
for i < 10, modulo constants. The saved GAP row actions are transposed to
act on columns. Successive flag dimensions are 0,10,54,55,65,109,110,120.
These are concrete witness matrices, not an assumed composition series.
`MatrixChecks` checks the basis inverse and adapted action equations.
The native identification and irreducibility of the blocks are separate.

Source context: James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111; the degree reduction
used in Aschbacher–Smith, Chapter K, printed p.457. Discovery code and its
unchanged output are retained in `source/`. The packed matrix format follows
the existing M₂₂ Hermitian filtration implementation in this repository.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Representation.MathieuSmall.M12DegreeGap.InducedQuotients.CertificateData

abbrev Space := Fin 120 → ZMod 2
abbrev Factor := Fin 7

def cut (t : ℕ) : ℕ := ([0,10,54,55,65,109,110,120] : List ℕ)[t]?.getD 120

def degree (t : Factor) : ℕ := cut (t.val + 1) - cut t.val

theorem cut_zero : cut 0 = 0 := by decide +kernel

theorem cut_last : cut 7 = 120 := by decide +kernel

theorem cut_step : ∀ t : Factor, cut t.val < cut (t.val + 1) ∧ cut (t.val + 1) ≤ 120 :=
  by decide +kernel

theorem degree_allowed (t : Factor) : degree t ∈ ({1, 10, 44} : Set ℕ) := by
  have h : ∀ t : Factor, degree t = 1 ∨ degree t = 10 ∨ degree t = 44 := by decide +kernel
  exact h t

theorem degree_pos (t : Factor) : 0 < degree t := Nat.sub_pos_of_lt (cut_step t).1

def blockIndex (t : Factor) (x : Fin (degree t)) : Fin 120 :=
  ⟨cut t.val + x.val, by have hx := x.isLt; have ht := cut_step t; dsimp [degree] at hx; omega⟩

def bit (v x : ℕ) : ZMod 2 := if v.testBit x then 1 else 0

